#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:1
#: 969d759c2fe94ce984c2739d7a4ca678
msgid "Sphinx & Furo Sidebar Navigation Architecture (ADR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:3
#: 19a278afcef941dba0f4af7be6f12245
msgid ""
"This document records the technical feasibility analysis and Architecture"
" Decision Record (ADR) for expandable hierarchical heading navigation in "
"the Sphinx and Furo left sidebar (Issue "
"[#309](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/issues/309), Epic "
"[#379](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/issues/379))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:10
#: 3f23cceab225481baa4cdd7cd57178d2
msgid "1. Context & Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:12
#: 377bb2202485456a8b2ac674a08c77a0
msgid ""
"In standard Sphinx documentation built with the **Furo** theme, the left "
"navigation drawer (`.sidebar-tree`) displays only document-level titles, "
"while in-page headings (`H2`, `H3`) appear exclusively in the right-hand "
"\"On this page\" table of contents (`.toc-tree`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:16
#: 485d44c2068d48c78c6964c87df39440
msgid ""
"For multi-section reference documentation—such as **User Guides** "
"(`guides/index.md`), **CLI Reference** (`cli/index.md`), and **API "
"Reference** (`api/findfmt.md`)—readers could not expand a document entry "
"in the left sidebar to jump directly to nested sections or module anchors"
" without first loading the target page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:23
#: e3f0eeccbdb24052893df6e068aadebc
msgid "2. Technical Feasibility Investigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:25
#: 5c75c266f23146379e73761b755e2ed4
msgid "2.1. Sphinx `toctree` Resolution vs. Furo `titles_only` Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:27
#: f0e5f7dfdde644c3bef47db3355c249d
msgid ""
"Sphinx's `TocTree` adapter "
"(`sphinx.environment.adapters.toctree._resolve_toctree`) supports two "
"modes when constructing the global navigation tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:30
#: 45a5e7e3bc724849b158e5cc27d01fc4
msgid ""
"**`titles_only=True`**: Emits only top-level document titles (`H1`), "
"ignoring all in-page subsections regardless of `:maxdepth:` directives in"
" MyST Markdown sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:32
#: 2982aaa8f7c64f92b51270866aee3d1d
msgid ""
"**`titles_only=False`**: Includes nested document headings (`H2`, `H3`, "
"`H4`) and Python autodoc object anchors up to the active `maxdepth` "
"ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:35
#: 590d6aeb56d14a348627cc2a1f42f4ff
msgid ""
"By default, Furo's `_compute_navigation_tree(context)` function in "
"`furo/__init__.py` hardcodes `titles_only=True`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:47
#: 92c6c6966da9439db3ebdf9bbaff851f
msgid ""
"Because `titles_only=True` is passed directly to Sphinx's `toctree()` "
"template callable, increasing `:maxdepth:` in `docs/source/index.md` or "
"section index files alone has no effect on Furo's left sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:51
#: f2763ada840f40c283dd8945f486a49b
msgid "2.2. Furo Navigation Tree Post-Processing (`get_navigation_tree`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:53
#: 52ed313b233f46539ee1f922eab077d6
msgid ""
"Furo transforms Sphinx's raw `toctree` HTML via "
"`furo.navigation.get_navigation_tree(toctree_html)`. Inspection of "
"`furo.navigation` confirms that this post-processor is completely depth-"
"agnostic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:56
#: 3b42bbf8a3314b87bd0db42fb5815172
msgid ""
"It parses the `toctree` HTML fragment with `BeautifulSoup` and iterates "
"recursively over every `<li>` element (`soup.find_all(\"li\", "
"recursive=True)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:58
#: b7057cfd2c1948bc98e482bc8dc702dc
msgid ""
"Whenever an `<li>` element contains a child `<ul>` (whether that `<ul>` "
"represents child documents or nested in-page headings), Furo appends the "
"`has-children` CSS class, injects an `<input type=\"checkbox\" class"
"=\"toctree-checkbox\" role=\"switch\" aria-label=\"Toggle navigation of "
"...\">`, and inserts a `<label>` containing the `#svg-arrow-right` "
"expand/collapse chevron icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:62
#: 056e35faf97847dca18a0088fd65e6ba
msgid ""
"Any `<li>` along the active document ancestry carrying the `current` "
"class has its checkbox marked `checked=\"\"` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/sidebar_navigation.md:64
#: 3090f537f9e948f6b1cf6c6417b2976e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Furo's CSS rules (`.toctree-checkbox ~ ul { display: none; }` and "
"`.toctree-checkbox:checked ~ ul { display: block; }`) operate on general "
"sibling selectors and therefore support arbitrary nesting depths "
"(`toctree-l1` through `toctree-l4`)."
msgstr ""

